cess","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Framework:** compare total cost, time to market and control across expected fund count and asset trajectory.\n\n**Series trust (white-label):**\n- Existing board, CCO, auditor, administrator, custodian and exemptive/Rule 6c-11 infrastructure make launch faster and cheaper.\n- Costs are mostly per-fund or asset-based, often with minimum fees. These can become expensive at scale.\n- **Control trade-off:** the platform's board and adviser usually oversee you. They can terminate or replace you, and they shape service providers, policies and timing. Your brand may also share governance risk with unrelated funds.\n\n**Own trust:**\n- Gives full control over board composition, vendors and future product lineup.\n- Requires substantial upfront legal costs, board and CCO costs, longer setup, and fixed costs that one fund must bear.\n\n**Deciding factors:** realistic AUM and break-even, any plans for more funds, the strategy's complexity, distribution relationships and tolerance for oversight.\n\nFor most single-fund, budget-limited sponsors, a series trust is a reasonable starting point. Negotiate exit and reorganization terms upfront. Get current fee quotes and legal advice.","ttft_ms":1841,"type":"result","duration_ms":6131,"uuid":"0f900184-291e-4a94-a31e-bbf3bfc48e44","ttft_stream_ms":1357,"time_to_request_ms":69,"first_content_frame_ms":1357,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
